---Archive an agent
---
---Archives the agent under the same If-Match precondition as a replace (428 missing, 412 stale). Send no body, or an empty object. The version does not change but the ETag does; history stays readable, the record leaves the default list, and further writes, including a second archive, return 409. Needs no repository push. Restore it with POST .../agents/{id}/restore. Requires canManageAgents (automation principals require project write or manage). Route requests to the project's API URL returned by Core.
---
---`POST /api/v1/{host}/{project}/agents/{id}/archive`
---@param input entire.agents.ArchiveProjectAgentRequest
---@return entire.agents.Agent? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:archive_project_agent(input) end

---Claim a self-hosted agent run
---
---Claims the run for the calling service account and starts it: it is running until its result arrives or its deadline passes. A run still waiting is checked against its branch: if the branch moved past the run's commit, the run is canceled as superseded and the claim is refused as run_not_claimable; an unreadable branch is a 503. A run the account already holds, still running and before its deadline, is returned again unchanged, so a claim whose response was lost can be retried. Every call, held runs included, re-checks that the account is bound to the run's Environment, is a member of the run's repository with pull on it, and that the repository is not paused; an account that lost access never gets the prompt again. 404 run_not_found: the run is unknown or the caller may not see it. 409: run_claimed (another account holds it), run_not_claimable (it is no longer waiting) or repository_paused. The route is not scoped to a project: bindings say which Environments the account serves, and a runner talks to the cell that processes its project's repositories. Needs a service account token.
---
---`POST /api/v1/self-hosted-runner/jobs/{run_id}/claim`
---@param input entire.agents.ClaimSelfHostedRunnerRequest
---@return entire.agents.SelfHostedRunClaim? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:claim_self_hosted_runner(input) end

---Complete a claimed self-hosted agent run
---
---Validates the result with the checks a hosted run's result gets and publishes it as the run's review. A result that does not parse, or whose findings point at files absent from the reviewed commit, is a 422 that leaves the run claimed, so the runner can correct it and post again before the deadline. 404 when the run is not one this account claimed; 409 when the run has finished, timed out, been canceled, or its Change moved past the reviewed commit. Needs a service account token.
---
---`POST /api/v1/self-hosted-runner/runs/{run_id}/complete`
---@param input entire.agents.CompleteSelfHostedRunnerRequest
---@return entire.agents.SelfHostedRunCompleted? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:complete_self_hosted_runner(input) end

---Create an agent
---
---Saves a new agent in the project at version 1 and returns it with its JSON etag write token, HTTP ETag and Location. Saving runs nothing. Send preset for an Entire preset with its environment, repository_ids, triggers and is_enabled, or every field and a name for a custom agent. Send environment_id, environment (saved in the same transaction as an ordinary, reusable project record; any refusal saves nothing) or runs_on self_hosted alone (the project's managed self-hosted environment). runs_on may accompany environment_id or environment when it equals that environment's runs_on, so an agent read can be sent back; a mismatch is 422. Agent names are unique among the project's active agents, ignoring case, and a project runs each preset at most once among its active agents (409 otherwise). It selects repositories of the project and requires repository push on each, recorded as repository_added events. Saving starts no run. Idempotency-Key is required: a retry with the same key and body saves nothing and returns the agent the first attempt saved, at its current version, with Idempotency-Replayed: true; the same key with a different body returns 409. A key is scoped to the caller, the project and agents, and does not expire. Bodies use the typed request schema; unknown fields, including spec wrappers and server-owned fields, are refused. Requires canManageAgents (automation principals require project write or manage). Route requests to the project's API URL returned by Core.
---
---`POST /api/v1/{host}/{project}/agents`
---@param input entire.agents.CreateProjectAgentRequest
---@return entire.agents.Agent? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_project_agent(input) end

