---Pause an agent
---
---Sets is_enabled, paused_at and paused_by. Stops its trigger and cancels its queued and running runs; manual runs still work. Needs no repository push: pausing only stops runs. Send If-Match (428 missing, 412 stale) and no body. Already in that state returns 200 and changes nothing. Stale repositories do not block it. An archived agent returns 409. Requires canManageAgents (automation principals require project write or manage). Route requests to the project's API URL returned by Core.
---
---`POST /api/v1/{host}/{project}/agents/{id}/pause`
---@param input entire.agents.PauseProjectAgentRequest
---@return entire.agents.Agent? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:pause_project_agent(input) end

---Replace an agent
---
---Replaces every editable field as a new immutable version; omitted optional fields take their defaults. Send If-Match with the JSON etag value of the last read or write: missing returns 428 and stale returns 412. An archived agent returns 409. Every field, as for a create, with environment_id or runs_on self_hosted alone; runs_on may accompany environment_id when it equals the environment's runs_on, so an agent read can be sent back. A preset agent's name, model, instructions and signal are the preset's: a replace that sends different ones is refused (422); send preset null with every field to customize the agent under the same id. It saves a version only when what the agent runs changes; repository_ids is applied as adds and removes. is_enabled, if sent, must match the agent's state (422 agent_state_not_replaceable). Requires push on each repository it adds, and on each one it keeps when it saves a version, departed ones included. Removing a repository needs no push. Requires canManageAgents (automation principals require project write or manage). Route requests to the project's API URL returned by Core.
---
---`PUT /api/v1/{host}/{project}/agents/{id}`
---@param input entire.agents.ReplaceProjectAgentRequest
---@return entire.agents.Agent? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:replace_project_agent(input) end

---Restore an agent
---
---Makes an archived agent active again, paused or not as it was. Send If-Match (428 missing, 412 stale) and no body. Its name and preset must still be free among the project's active agents (409 otherwise), its environment must still be active (422 otherwise), and restoring an active agent returns 409. Needs no repository push: it runs again only as already approved. Requires canManageAgents (automation principals require project write or manage). Route requests to the project's API URL returned by Core.
---
---`POST /api/v1/{host}/{project}/agents/{id}/restore`
---@param input entire.agents.RestoreProjectAgentRequest
---@return entire.agents.Agent? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:restore_project_agent(input) end

---Resume an agent
---
---Sets is_enabled, paused_at and paused_by. Lets its trigger run it again; 422 when its saved version can no longer run. Needs no repository push: it runs again only as already approved. Send If-Match (428 missing, 412 stale) and no body. Already in that state returns 200 and changes nothing. Stale repositories do not block it. An archived agent returns 409. Requires canManageAgents (automation principals require project write or manage). Route requests to the project's API URL returned by Core.
---
---`POST /api/v1/{host}/{project}/agents/{id}/resume`
---@param input entire.agents.ResumeProjectAgentRequest
---@return entire.agents.Agent? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:resume_project_agent(input) end

